(EXP-32: `is greater than`.
 Also covers: EXP-33 `is less than`, EXP-34 `is equal to`, EXP-35 the bare
 `x is 0` value comparison, EXP-36 `the` being optional before a variable name
 in a comparison.
 Each comparison is run in both polarities so a leaf writing an assertion on
 one of them knows the false branch is reached too.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox EXP-32.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   x over 5
   y not over 5
   y under 10
   x not under 3
   lhs equals rhs
   lhs differs from x
   origin is 0
   x is not 0
)
a number called x is 7.
a number called y is 3.
a number called lhs is 4.
a number called rhs is 4.
a number called origin is 0.
If the x is greater than 5 then, Print "x over 5". Otherwise, Print "x not over 5".
If the y is greater than 5 then, Print "y over 5". Otherwise, Print "y not over 5".
If y is less than 10 then, Print "y under 10". Otherwise, Print "y not under 10".
If x is less than 3 then, Print "x under 3". Otherwise, Print "x not under 3".
If lhs is equal to rhs then, Print "lhs equals rhs". Otherwise, Print "lhs differs".
If lhs is equal to x then, Print "lhs equals x". Otherwise, Print "lhs differs from x".
If origin is 0 then, Print "origin is 0". Otherwise, Print "origin is not 0".
If x is 0 then, Print "x is 0". Otherwise, Print "x is not 0".
